        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "Identity and page check: the held text for EO 6321 is the American Presidency Project transcription (APP node 362146), registered as grade mirror_transcription (not an original). Its page record is a Common Crawl capture of 2025-09-06T08:31:47Z whose heading names Executive Order 6321, whose date (October 3, 1933) and subject agree with the text, and whose text sha256 equals the held text's. The WPA 1944 list row (1933 Oct 3 p.542: Code of Fair Competition for the Motor Vehicle Retailing Trade approved. I NRA Codes 563.) confirms the order's date and subject. The order approves a code of fair competition under section 3(a) of Title I of the National Industrial Recovery Act, so the reviewed shared analysis (SHARED_ANALYSIS.md and review-shared/ADJUDICATION.json) applies: a code-dependent command that did not end earlier ended on June 14, 1935 by statutory repeal (S.J. Res. 113 sec. 2); Schechter (May 27, 1935) is a validity characterization, not an end date. No inventory correction was needed: the one machine clause is the operative paragraph and the preamble only recites the application, hearings and findings.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"The order states no period, condition, \\\"until\\\" date or provisional approval of its own. Searched the held order texts (jobs/*/output/texts, through the Cruden lookup and a follow-up regex search on the code's name), the census register and the WPA 1944 list for later orders citing EO 6321 by number or naming its code: no held order text cites EO 6321 by number. EO 6948 (January 18, 1935), which approves the Code of Fair Competition for the Motor Vehicle Maintenance Trade, names this code: it stays the maintenance code's provisions for sixty days as to retailers insofar as they conflict with this code and directs a later determination by the National Industrial Recovery Board of which provisions of the two codes prevail. That later order leaves this approval in place and no held determination modifies or revokes it, so it is a later event, not an end. No held record shows this code cancelled, modified under section 10(b), superseded, revoked or suspended before June 14, 1935. June 16, 1935 is not an end: section 1 of S.J. Res. 113 replaced the original two-year expiry with April 1, 1936.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"The order contains no appointment, direction to an agency, delegation under another statute or other command independent of the code; the \\\"Approval recommended\\\" line records a recommendation, not a command.\",\"savings_check\":\"Savings reviewed under NIRA section 5 and S.J. Res. 113 section 2 and its proviso: accrued acts, liabilities and any completed-action exemption under the Code of Fair Competition for the Motor Vehicle Retailing Trade are preserved as accrued effects; nothing continues the approval, and no held source shows a prosecution or enforcement continued after June 14, 1935.\",\"scope_check\":\"One operative clause (chars 735-1197), the approval of the Code of Fair Competition for the Motor Vehicle Retailing Trade. The order states no condition, exception, stay, exemption or period.\"}",
